    "4.1": `<p>Three alkenes can be drawn for this bromide: <b>A</b> by loss of the hydrogen on C1, and <b>B and C</b> by loss of the one on C3. The more substituted ones, B and C, are normally favoured. Which one forms is set by geometry.</p>`,
